{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42236 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "Poricoic Acid B is implicated in the interaction with Raji through multiple pathways, all leading to the same target, Raji. The evidence suggests that Poricoic Acid B acts as a target for MIP, which in turn is targeted by CID 21582484 and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, both of which target Raji. Additionally, Poricoic Acid B is also linked to Maplexin A, which also targets Raji. These findings collectively indicate that Poricoic Acid B may exert its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions, ultimately leading to the transformation or modulation of Raji cells. The consistent targeting of Raji by multiple entities suggests a potential mechanism involving the activation or inhibition of cellular processes within Raji, though the exact nature of these interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
